            %p Elementary as this example may be, it embdies some important principles:
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K} \,=\, \mathbb{C}
              the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+monad"} Frobenius monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Q}W \otimes (\text{-}) \,\colon\, \mathbb{C}Mod \to \mathbb{C}Mod
              (or rather
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                      %mi W
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mtext -
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi FinDimHilb
                      %mo →
                      %mi FinDimHilb
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Q}W \otimes (\text{-}) \,\colon\, FinDimHilb \to FinDimHilb
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "quantum+measurement#CoeckePavlović08"} Coecke &amp; Pavlović 2008
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement"} quantum measurement
              in the context of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+via+dagger-compact+categories"} quantum information via dagger-compact categories
              and is used as such in the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zxCalculus"} zxCalculus
              (where the Frobenius property is embodied by “spider diagrams”). Various authors discuss the Frobenius algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Q}W
              in this context, see the references
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "quantum+information+theory+via+dagger-compact+categories#MeasurementReferencesQuantumInformationTheoryViaStringDiagrams"} there
            %p
              From another perspective on the same phenomenon (discussed at
              = succeed "):" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+circuits+via+dependent+linear+types"} quantum circuits via dependent linear types
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Q}W
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/writer+monad"} writer monad
              underlying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+monad"} Frobenius monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Q}W \otimes (-) \,\colon\, \mathbb{K}Mod \to \mathbb{K}Mod
              is a linear version of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reader+monad"} reader monad
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+reader+monad"} quantum reader monad
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+in+computer+science"} computational effect
              its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+morphisms"} Kleisli morphisms
              encode
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gates"} quantum gates
              with an “indefiniteness”-effect (in the sense of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "necessity+and+possibility#ModalQuantumLogic"} quantum modal logic
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a{:href => "monad+in+computer+science#MonadModulesInIdeaSection"} handling
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement"} quantum measurement
            %p
              In particular, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras
              (hence also the corresponding
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra+over+a+comonad"} coalgebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Q}W \otimes (\text{-})
              the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+types"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  \-dependent
                  = succeed "-linear" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕂
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+sets"} indexed sets
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces+of+quantum+states"} spaces of quantum states
              after
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state+collapse"} collapse
              following the measurement result
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in W
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A Frobenius algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} object dual
              to itself.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              be the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+unit"} monoidal unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is dual to itself means there are maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e: I \to A \otimes A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p: A \otimes A \to I
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identities"} triangle identities
              hold. The maps are defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi η
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi δ
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi μ
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e = (I \stackrel{\eta}{\to} A \stackrel{\delta}{\to} A \otimes A), \qquad p = (A \otimes A \stackrel{\mu}{\to} A \stackrel{\epsilon}{\to} I)
            %p
              and one of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identities"} triangle identities
              uses one of the Frobenius laws and unit and counit axioms to derive the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+diagram"} commutative diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi δ
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi A
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi μ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi μ
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi δ
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp; \stackrel{1 \otimes \eta}{\to} &amp; A \otimes A &amp; \stackrel{1 \otimes \delta}{\to} &amp; A \otimes A \otimes A \\
                    \&amp; {}_1\searrow &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\mu} &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\mu \otimes 1} \\
                    \&amp; &amp; A &amp; \overset{\delta}{\to} &amp; A \otimes A \\
                    \&amp; &amp;  &amp; {}_{1}\searrow &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\epsilon \otimes 1} \\
                    \&amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; A
                    }
            %p
              The other
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identity"} triangle identity
              uses the other Frobenius law and unit and counit axioms.
          %p
            As a result, we see that in the monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_k
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            considered as modules over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+module"} finitely generated
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes_k -
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint
            to itself, is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints+preserve+colimits"} therefore preserves all colimits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi k
                  %mo −
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes_k -
            preserves arbitrary small coproducts means
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is finitely generated over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi k
                  %mo −
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes_k-
            preserves coequalizers means
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is projective over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every Frobenius algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-Frobenius+algebra"} quasi-Frobenius algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                coincide.
            %li
              %p
                Every Frobenius algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                = succeed ":" do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    pseudo-Frobenius algebra
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/pseudo-Frobenius+algebra"} ?
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is an injective cogenerator in the category of left (right)
                = succeed "-modules." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Frobenius algebras are closely connected with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ambidextrous+adjunctions"} ambidextrous adjunctions
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+monad"} Frobenius monad
            on a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is by definition a Frobenius monoid in the monoidal category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (with monoidal product given by endofunctor composition), and if we have a pair of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \dashv U
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \dashv F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = U F
            carries a monad structure and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            structure and the Frobenius laws are satisfied, a fact most easily seen by using
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
          %h3#props_for_frobenius_algebras PROPs for Frobenius algebras
          %p
            Certain kinds of Frobenius algebras have nice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PROPs"} PROPs
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PRO"} PROs
            %a{:href => "#Lauda2006"} Lauda (2006)
            and illustrated here:
          %p
            %img{:alt => "string diagrams for the Frobenius algebra axioms", :src => "/nlab/files/frobenius_algebra.jpg"}/
          %p
            Lauda and Pfeiffer
            %a{:href => "#Lauda2008"} Lauda (2008)
            showed that the PROP for
            %em symmetric
            Frobenius algebras is the category of ‘topological open strings’, since it obeys this extra axiom:
          %p
            %img{:alt => "string diagram for the \"symmetric\" law in a Frobenius algebra", :src => "/nlab/files/symmetric_frobenius_algebra_law.jpg"}/
          %p
            The PROP for
            %em commutative
            Frobenius algebras is
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                2Cob
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/2Cob"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Abrams96"} Abrams (1996)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            %a{:href => "#Kock2006"} Kock (2006)
            for a history of this subject and
            %a{:href => "#Kock2004"} Kock (2004)
            for a detailed introduction. In 2Cob, the circle is a Frobenius algebra. The monoid laws look like this:
          %p
            %img{:alt => "diagrams for the monoid laws in 2Cob", :src => "/nlab/files/monoid_laws.jpg"}/
          %p The comonoid laws look like this:
          %p
            %img{:alt => "diagrams for the comonoid laws in 2Cob", :src => "/nlab/files/comonoid_laws.jpg"}/
          %p The Frobenius laws look like this:
          %p
            %img{:alt => "diagrams for the Frobenius laws in 2Cob", :src => "/nlab/files/frobenius_laws.jpg"}/
          %p and the commutative law looks like this:
          %p
            %img{:alt => "diagrams for the commutative law in 2Cob", :src => "/nlab/files/commutative_law.jpg"}/
          %p
            The PROP for
            %em special
            commutative Frobenius algebras is Cospan(FinSet), as proved by Rosebrugh, Sabadini and Walters. This is worth comparing to the PROP for commutative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bialgebra"} bialgebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Rosebrugh2005"} Rosebrugh et al (2005)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lack2004"} Lack (2004)
          %p
            A special commutative Frobenius algebra gives a 2d TQFT that is insensitive to the genus of a 2-manifold, since in terms of pictures, the ‘specialness’ axioms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi δ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \circ \delta = 1
            says that
          %p
            %img{:alt => "string diagram for the \"special\" law in a Frobenius algebra", :src => "/nlab/files/special_law.jpg"}/
